module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "import_only_walker_standing_in_for_the_closure_authority" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a consumer that needs a MODULE CLOSURE -- every module the subject depends on -- is answered by an import-line BFS (extract_import_paths, parse-tree import params, or an adjacency built only from ImportResolutionFact). A provider reached only by a qualified or bare reference is omitted. The compile, skip-set, regen, or fixture then proceeds over a strict subset of the one closure authority (v1_compiler.cli_run extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint: import edges PLUS dotted-reference PLUS bare-reference, to a joint fixpoint). HARM: unresolved-type / undefined-variable against a module that resolves in every authority-built closure, or a skip-set that does not skip when a reference-only provider changes.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE. Classify by what the CONSUMER means, never by the walker's name. If the consumer compiles, typechecks, evaluates, skips, regenerates, or otherwise treats membership as 'everything this module depends on', the walk must be the one closure authority (or the v2 equivalent), never a second BFS over import lines. If the consumer means the authored import graph itself -- layer_import_facts, exclusion-orphan walls, import-syntax presence, a test hook named declared-import-closure-only -- leave it, with that reason stated beside it. policy_entry_closure_sources is NOT in that leave set: its consumers compile and evaluate gunbc.compile_clean_diagnostic_policy, so membership is a source closure. Two hits made it a class: gunbc#13437 (resolve_virtual_source_with_imports, the fixture closure) and gunbc#13464 (entry_resolve::import_closure_dag_files, the Class B skip-set). Both now seed from declared entries and route through extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint; #13464 keeps a test-only import-line mutant that must omit the reference-only provider.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: this is not 'imports are incomplete'. An import line, a qualified reference and a bare reference are the SAME dependency edge in this namespace. An import-only walk is not a narrower closure but a blind one. Nor is it entry_closure_admits_modules_the_entry_does_not_use (over-closure via the bare census); this class is UNDER-closure. A walker that already calls the authority after an import-line seed (primary_root_subject_closure via resolve_transitively_bfs_legacy then extend, regen_input_sources_over_roots, resolve_virtual_source_with_imports after #13437) is not a second authority. resolve_transitively_bfs_legacy is that shared import-edge seed helper, not a compile-subject loader of its own.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 2, mechanically preventable, on the two repaired production paths -- each carries a discriminating RED (a provider reached only by reference is a member), a test-only mutant that reverts to imports-only and fails that RED, and a positive control that a real error in the closure still refuses -- and those tests run on a small fixture tree, not the live corpus. THE CLASS AS A WHOLE SITS AT THE MINIMUM ACROSS ITS IN-SCOPE PATHS (DESIGN section 4b(1)): remaining compile-subject loaders in the seed (policy_entry_closure_sources, v1/tests helpers resolve_imports_transitively, compiler_tests resolve_source_closure, the four stage0 witness bins' duplicate import BFS, v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_resolve_transitively_fn writing the same walker into generated crates) still answer closure with import lines, so a silent under-close remains writable there. Reporting the whole class at 2 would be inflation. Honest standing of the UNREPAIRED paths is mitigatable: the wrong answer is loud when the omitted provider is demanded, but nothing structurally stops a new import-only BFS from being bound as a compile closure.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Closure membership for a compile subject is decidable from the same three channels the authority already iterates; a second import-line BFS is a fork, not a missing fact. Ceiling is not 4 while the seed may still write a VecDeque over extract_import_paths.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, at capability grain: every compile-subject loader is derived from the one closure-extension authority (extend_sources_to_both_closure_fixpoint, or the v2 producer that is that relation), so an import-line BFS cannot be bound as a compile closure. WHAT DOES NOT SATISFY IT: grepping for extract_import_paths (the scanner is legitimate for the import-graph consumers named above); routing one more call site while the emitted crate still ships resolve_transitively_with_seen; or a lens that flags BFS without naming the consumer's meaning. The population is an identity join over every extract_import_paths caller and every named import-edge walker (see PR #13510 body for the derivation command), not a sample.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster. It does not retire the remaining walkers; each closure-meaning site is its own follow-up with the same RED/mutant/control shape.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
